course: dictionary
lesson: 13598
title: Words that show trouble and timing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something happened, not just what happened. Read this: «The bus broke down inconveniently in the rain.» The bus broke down, and the rain makes it worse. Inconveniently tells you the breakdown caused trouble at a bad time or in a bad place.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. Trouble words often sit next to things that go wrong, like breaking down, closing, or getting in the way. Ask yourself: was this easy, or was it a problem? If it was a problem, the word probably means something like awkward or at a bad time.
explain: You can check your idea by swapping in a simple phrase. «The bus broke down at a bad time in the rain» still makes sense, so your meaning is right. Always test the meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word.
fact: Inconveniently is an adverb, so it tells you how something happened.
fact: «Inconveniently» means in a way that causes trouble or difficulty, or at a bad time.
fact: «The bus broke down inconveniently in the rain.» Being stuck in the rain makes the trouble worse.
fact: «The shop closed inconveniently early, before we could buy the cake.» The closing time was a problem for them.
fact: Inconveniently often appears in phrases like «inconveniently placed» or «inconveniently timed», meaning in the wrong spot or at the wrong moment.
exercise: «The bus broke down inconveniently in the rain.» What does inconveniently mean here? | In a funny way that made everyone laugh | *Politely, with a smile | In a way that causes trouble, at a bad time | Very slowly and quietly
exercise: Mum says the party was inconveniently timed, because it clashed with our football match. What does inconveniently timed mean? | Timed exactly the same as every other party | Timed so it was early and quick | Timed to be the best party ever | *Timed at a bad moment that causes a problem
exercise: «The sofa was inconveniently placed, right in front of the door.» Where is the problem? | The sofa is very soft and comfy | The sofa is far away in the garden | The sofa is painted bright red | *The sofa blocks the way in and out
test: «The train was cancelled inconveniently, just as we reached the station.» What does inconveniently mean here? | In a happy and helpful way | In a quiet and careful way | *In a way that caused trouble, at a bad time | Very early in the morning
test: Leo says the rain came inconveniently just after we had washed the car. Why is inconveniently the right word? | Because the rain was warm and gentle | Because the rain was a surprise that everyone enjoyed | *Because the rain caused trouble at a bad time | Because the rain stopped quickly
exam: «The lift stopped inconveniently between the second and third floors.» Which word tells you the stop was a problem? | lift | *inconveniently | stopped | floors
